Root cause:
In irdma_create_qp, the initialization of `iwqp->free_qp` was placed after the `udata` block containing `ib_copy_to_udata`. If that copy call failed, the error path invoked `irdma_destroy_qp` which attempted to wait on the `free_qp` completion before it had been initialized, causing a use-before-initialization bug.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>
init_completion(&iwqp->free_qp);  // originally placed after the udata block (line removed)
</text>
<text>
if (err_code) { ibdev_dbg(...); irdma_destroy_qp(&iwqp->ibqp, udata); return err_code; }
</text>
Reason:
The completion `iwqp->free_qp` is initialized after the udata block. If `ib_copy_to_udata` fails, the error path calls `irdma_destroy_qp` which waits on this completion before it has been initialized, causing a use-before-initialization bug.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>
+	init_completion(&iwqp->free_qp);
</text>
Reason:
Moving `init_completion` before the udata block ensures that the completion is fully initialized before any code path that might use it, including the error path of `ib_copy_to_udata`. Thus, when `irdma_destroy_qp` is called, the completion is already initialized and can be safely waited on.


